dhakrishnan, Chao-Han Huck Yang, Sumeer Ahmad Khan, Rohit Kumar, Narsis A Kiani,\n1031\tDavid Gomez-Cabrero, and Jesper Tegner. Whispering LLaMA: A cross-modal generative error correction\n1032\tframework for speech recognition. In Proceedings of the Conference on Empirical Methods in Natural\n1033\tLanguage Processing (EMNLP), 2023.\n1034\t[45] Nils Reimers and Iryna Gurevych. Sentence-bert: Sentence embeddings using siamese bert-networks.\n1035\tIn Proceedings of the 2019 conference on empirical methods in natural language processing and the 9th\n1036\tinternational joint conference on natural language processing (EMNLP-IJCNLP), pp. 3982–3992, 2019.\n1037\t[46] Dima Rekesh, Nithin Rao Koluguri, Samuel Kriman, Somshubra Majumdar, Vahid Noroozi, He Huang,\n1038\tOleksii Hrinchuk, Krishna Puvvada, Ankur Kumar, Jagadeesh Balam, et al. Fast conformer with linearly\n1039\tscalable attention for efficient speech recognition. In 2023 IEEE Automatic Speech Recognition and\n1040\tUnderstanding Workshop (ASRU), pp. 1–8. IEEE, 2023.\n1041\t[47] Julian Salazar, Davis Liang, Toan Q. Nguyen, and Katrin Kirchhoff. Masked language model scoring.\n1042\tIn Proceedings of the 58th Annual Meeting of the Association for Computational Linguistics (ACL), pp.\n1043\t2699–2712, 2020.\n1044\t\n1045\t13\n1046\t\n1047\t\fVoice Memory for Agentic Speech Recognition\n1048\t\n1049\t[48] Sonya M Sheffert and Carol A Fowler. The effects of voice and visible speaker change on memory for\n1050\tspoken words. Journal of Memory and Language, 34(5):665–685, 1995.\n1051\t[49] Andreas Stolcke, Klaus Ries, Noah Coccaro, Elizabeth Shriberg, Rebecca Bates, Daniel Jurafsky, Paul\n1052\tTaylor, Rachel Martin, Carol Van Ess-Dykema, and Marie Meteer. Dialog act modeling for automatic\n1053\ttagging and recognition of conversational speech. Computational Linguisitics, 26(3):339, 2000.\n1054\t[50] Piotr Szymański, Piotr Żelasko, Mikolaj Morzy, Adrian Szymczak, Marzena Zyła-Hoppe, et al. WER we\n1055\tare and WER